{
  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development is unacceptable in\r\nprinciple, whereby the proposed subdivision of commercial space for residential\r\ndevelopment at ground floor level fails to contribute&nbsp;to the vitality and\r\nviability of the District Town Centre contrary to Policy(s) and 40 and 41 of\r\nthe Waltham Forest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The proposed self contained residential unit,\r\ndue to its poor layout creates a cramped form of living environment, failing to\r\nmeet minimum space standards as well as failing to achieve good quality housing\r\nfor future occupants contrary to Policy(s) 53 and 56&nbsp;of the Waltham Forest\r\nadopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "Due to insufficient information in relation to\r\nthe location of internal or external refuse storage, an adequate assessment\r\ncould not be made whether adequate facilities for the storage of refuse and\r\nrecycling have been provided for the proposed residential unit contrary to\r\nPolicy 57&nbsp;of the Waltham Forest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "Due to insufficient information in relation to\r\nthe provision of secure cycle storage, an adequate assessment could not be made\r\nwhether adequate facilities for secure cycle storage have been provided contrary\r\nto Policy 61 and Appendix 1 – Parking Standards of the Waltham Forest adopted\r\nLocal Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The applicant has failed to enter\r\ninto a S106 agreement and therefore not in compliance with Policy 94&nbsp;of\r\nthe Waltham Forest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024), specifically in relation to\r\nthe following planning obligations requirements (figures applicable at the time\r\nof the assessment of the application).&nbsp;\r\n\r\n\r\n Financial contribution of £627.00 towards the\r\n     Epping Forest SAMM.\r\n"
  ],
